        "e": "<strong>Trastuzumab mechanism of action and multi-omics data interpretation (Topic 641):</strong> Analyzing Table 1 demonstrates the multi-omics effects of the humanized monoclonal antibody trastuzumab in SK-BR-3 cells:<br>1. **Southern Blot:** The *HER2* / *GAPDH* genomic DNA ratio is unchanged (8.4 in vehicle vs 8.3 in trastuzumab), confirming trastuzumab does not alter genomic gene copy number.<br>2. **Northern Blot:** Relative mRNA abundance remains unchanged (12.2 in vehicle vs 11.9 in trastuzumab), proving trastuzumab does not inhibit transcription or stimulate mRNA degradation.<br>3. **Western Blot:** Total HER2 protein drops substantially from 15.8 to 6.2, and autophosphorylated active HER2 (p-Tyr1248) plunges from 18.4 down to 2.1.<br>Trastuzumab binds to the extracellular domain IV of HER2, sterically preventing receptor dimerization, suppressing downstream kinase autophosphorylation, and triggering receptor endocytosis and lysosomal degradation without modifying DNA or mRNA levels.<br><br><em>Distractor Traps:</em><br>&bull; A is biologically impossible; monoclonal antibodies are extracellular macromolecular immunoglobulins that do not enter the nucleus to alter genomic copy numbers.<br>&bull; C is contradicted by Table 1; Northern blot mRNA levels remained unchanged after trastuzumab treatment (12.2 vs 11.9 rel. mRNA).<br>&bull; D describes ribonuclease action or RNAi, not monoclonal antibody-mediated receptor inhibition and endocytic degradation."
